cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  pm25forecast: multi-strategy deep ensembles for 48-hour urban PM2.5
  forecasting
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the
  associated paper.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dadras
    given-names: Sina
repository-code: "https://github.com/sinadadras021/pm25-ensemble-forecasting"
abstract: >-
  A configuration-driven, leakage-audited implementation comparing six
  ensemble strategies for 48-hour PM2.5 forecasting: statistical averaging
  (simple and SLSQP performance-weighted), non-linear meta-learning (MLP
  and gradient-boosted trees) and context-aware selection (hourly model
  output statistics and a random-forest model selector), over four deep
  base learners trained with inverse-weighted and exponential-extreme
  losses.
keywords:
  - air quality
  - PM2.5
  - deep learning
  - ensemble learning
  - stacking
  - time series forecasting
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
